From c692904b737cf94265eae4e22a474e3ed281a14a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hasan Mehdi <hasanthemehdi@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 10:15:41 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10/15] bt: Bluetooth service (power, scan, pair, connect,
 reconnect, sink)

Replaces the debug-menu test code. A control thread owns the radio;
calls return at once and bt_get_status reports progress. No panics on
runtime failures: they're logged to /.coda/bt.log (or /bt.log) and shown.

- Paired devices + names, last device, power and volumes persist in
  .rockbox/bt_devices.txt; the radio comes back on at boot and
  reconnects; we stay connectable so headphones can reconnect to us.
- Link lost (abnormal) -> 3 reconnect tries; audio pauses on any drop.
- The sink declares PCM_SINK_SWVOL (0 meant HWVOL: full-level output),
  runs at the one rate negotiated (48 kHz when the headphones take it),
  rounds 24->16 bit, and drives START/SUSPEND as a small state machine
  (one command in flight, re-evaluated on each ack).
- Wired and Bluetooth keep separate volumes; a crash on Bluetooth can't
  leave wired headphones at the Bluetooth level.
- AVRCP PLAY/PAUSE are honoured as such, not as a toggle.

